From: pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
Subject: Always On Display and double tap to wake (de.yesman.neo aod, double-tap-wake)

With aod on, blanking the built-in panel only marks it off: the shell's blanked state, the screen
saver and the power button behave as with a blank panel, while the shell puts a black overlay on
it with the time, the date, the battery and one icon per app with notifications, dim grey, moving
a little every minute against burn-in. With double-tap-wake on, every touchscreen that has a
wake_gesture attribute (s6sy761) goes into its low power gesture mode while blanked; its double
tap comes as KEY_WAKEUP and wakes the screen like any key.
---
